  "summary": "All 479 tests pass and `python -m compileall app` is clean.\n\n**What I found first:** every endpoint and field in the shared contract already exists here with exactly those names and shapes — `/settings/users` (including `initialPassword`/`temporaryPassword` and `POST /{userId}/reset-password`), the `Invited|Active|Deactivated` status enum, the bare-array `/settings/notifications` and `/settings/integrations`, the `{items,totalCount,page,pageSize}` envelopes on users/approval-rules/audit-log, and the partial-body PUT toggle. So no renaming was needed; I left those files alone.\n\n**What I built** — the notification capability described in the instruction (UC6/UC7/UC11):\n\n- `app/services/notifications.py` (new): the single service all emails and in-app alerts go through. `dispatch(...)` reads the event's Email/In-App toggles from `tenant_notification_settings` (defaulting to On for an event the tenant has never saved), sends mail via stdlib `smtplib` when `SMTP_HOST` is configured and logs it otherwise, and records the in-app alert as a `tenant_audit_log` entry with `log_action = \"Notification\"`. It never raises: a send failure is logged and written as a `NotificationFailed` audit entry, so the triggering action still completes. Callers invoke it after their own commit.\n- `app/config.py`: SMTP settings read from the environment (no hard-coded credentials, no new dependency).\n- `app/repositories/settings_notifications.py`: added the four event rows the new events need — `Contract Sent Back`, `Contract Ready for Signature`, `Contract Signature Declined`, `New User Invited` — alongside the existing seven. Seeding stays idempotent.\n- Wired the eight events: approve/reject/send back and ready-for-signature in `app/services/approvals.py` (`submit_action`); signing link in `app/services/signers.py` (`send_for_signature`) and again for the next signer in turn; executed and decline in `app/services/signing_sessions.py`; new user invite in `app/services/settings_users.py` (`create_user` — the temporary password is deliberately not mailed).\n- `tests/test_notifications.py` (new): default-on, both-toggles-off, and email-failure-is-logged-but-never-raises.\n\nTwo constraints worth stating: there is no `in_app_notifications` table in any module contract and `alembic/` is outside the paths I may modify, so in-app alerts land in the existing tenant-scoped `tenant_audit_log` rather than a new table. Rendering those alerts in a bell/inbox UI is the frontend's side.",
